1
00:02:35,294 --> 00:02:41,294
A new hero finds his roar!

2
00:05:10,588 --> 00:05:16,588
The Lion Guard: Return of the Roar is a family, tv movie,
animation film directed by Howy Parkins.

3
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:51,882
Set in the African savannah, the film follows Kion as he
assembles the members of the 'Lion Guard'.

4
00:10:21,176 --> 00:10:27,176
Throughout the film, the diverse team of young animals will learn how to utilize each of their unique abilities to solve problems and accomplish tasks to
maintain balance within the Circle of Life, while also introducing viewers to the vast array of animals that populate the prodigious African landscape.

5
00:12:56,470 --> 00:13:02,470
Kion (voice), played by Max Charles.

6
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:37,764
Bunga (voice), played by Joshua Rush.

7
00:18:07,058 --> 00:18:13,058
Zuri (voice), played by Madison Pettis.

8
00:20:42,352 --> 00:20:48,352
Janja (voice), played by Andrew Kishino.

9
00:23:17,647 --> 00:23:23,647
Cheezi (voice), played by Vargus Mason.

10
00:25:52,941 --> 00:25:58,941
Simba (voice), played by Rob Lowe.

11
00:28:28,235 --> 00:28:34,235
The Lion Guard is an American animated children's television series developed by
Ford Riley and based on Disney Animation's 1994 film The Lion King.

12
00:31:03,529 --> 00:31:09,529
The series was first broadcast with a television film titled The Lion Guard: Return of the Roar on Disney
Channel on November 22, 2015, and began airing as a TV series on January 15, 2016, on Disney Junior.

13
00:33:38,823 --> 00:33:44,823
It is the second television series based on The Lion King
following The Lion King's Timon & Pumbaa (1995–1999).

14
00:36:14,117 --> 00:36:20,117
The first two seasons take place within the time-gap in the
1998 film The Lion King II: Simba's Pride.

15
00:38:49,411 --> 00:38:55,411
The majority of the third and final season takes place in parallel with the film's
second act, with the final two episodes serving as an epilogue to the film.

16
00:41:24,705 --> 00:41:30,705
The second season premiered on July 7, 2017, followed by the third on August 3,
2019, with the series finale airing on November 3 the same year.
